WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.274
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Starfish Breath.

00:00:15.274 --> 00:00:22.547
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:22.547 --> 00:00:26.912
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:26.912 --> 00:00:31.276
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:31.276 --> 00:00:41.459
This is a breathing practice with a starfish shape. Hold up one hand, fingers spread wide — there is your starfish. Your other hand's pointer finger will do the tracing.

00:00:41.459 --> 00:00:53.097
Here is the shape: your tracing finger climbs up one finger while you breathe in, and slides down the other side while you breathe out. Up, in. Down, out. All five fingers, one whole starfish. You only ever trace your own hand.

00:00:53.097 --> 00:01:06.190
Either hand can be the starfish. And if a hand needs to rest, tracing the same starfish shape in the air or on your desk works exactly the same. The tracing is slow, and the breath follows it — no stopping, no holding at the fingertips.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:12.009
Nothing is ever held. The air moves in, the air moves out. That is the whole shape. Here we go.

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:25.101
First finger — the thumb. Trace up… breathing in. Trace down… breathing out.

00:01:25.101 --> 00:01:38.194
Next finger. Up… in. Down… out. Slow finger, easy breath.

00:01:38.194 --> 00:01:51.287
Middle finger, the tallest. Up… in. Down… out. Next finger. Up… in. Down… out.

00:01:51.287 --> 00:02:02.925
Last finger, the smallest. Up… in. Down… out. One whole starfish, finished.

00:02:02.925 --> 00:02:04.379
Now set both hands down on your desk. Let the tracing and the counting go, and just breathe the way your body wants to.

00:02:04.379 --> 00:02:17.472
Now hear the rules that keep this practice yours. The tracing is a gentle guide — it is never a test.

00:02:17.472 --> 00:02:30.565
If you lose your place, or trace a finger twice, your practice is still complete. Your breath, your pace. And this is never a contest — not the longest, not the quietest, not the slowest, not the biggest.

00:02:30.565 --> 00:02:40.748
And if anything ever feels dizzy, or tight, or strange, the move is simple: breathe normally. Normal breathing is always allowed, at any second. It is never a failure.

00:02:40.748 --> 00:02:42.203
Notice how your breathing feels now, all on its own. Nothing to fix. Nothing to hold.

00:02:42.203 --> 00:02:52.386
Up each finger, breathing in. Down, breathing out. Then let it be.

00:02:52.386 --> 00:02:59.660
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:05.479
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:03:05.479 --> 00:03:12.752
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:03:12.752 --> 00:03:20.026
You're ready for what's next.
